[CODE] STEP 1 — Install AsyncStorage.
  In your terminal (in the hydra folder):
      npx expo install @react-native-async-storage/async-storage

STEP 2 — Open App.js. Add at the top with the other imports:
      import { useEffect } from 'react';
      import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';

STEP 3 — Inside the App() function, right after the useState line, add:

      // Load saved state when the app opens
      useEffect(() => {
        AsyncStorage.getItem('hydra-glasses').then(saved => {
          if (saved) setGlasses(JSON.parse(saved));
        });
      }, []);

STEP 4 — Update the toggle function to also save:

      const toggle = (i) => {
        const next = [...glasses];
        next[i] = !next[i];
        setGlasses(next);
        AsyncStorage.setItem('hydra-glasses', JSON.stringify(next));
      };

STEP 5 — Test on your phone.
  Tap 3 glasses. Close Expo Go FULLY (swipe up).
  Reopen Expo Go, scan the QR again.
  YOU SHOULD SEE: the 3 glasses are STILL filled. State survived the close.

